'Altruism?'\nKejaan Kerrath says, 'If you continuously take from the life around you without ever giving back, eventually you'll find yourself with nothing left to take from. Think about this cavern, for example. Since you set foot here, you've disrupted its inhabitants. They were living quite peacefully until now. If you keep this up, you might eradicate some of the creatures and flora that grow only here. Why don't you try giving something [back] to them?'\nYou say, 'What would they want back?'\nKejaan Kerrath says, 'There's a beautiful variety of flower that I've only ever seen in these caves; I call them nightlight petunias. I worry they may wilt or be trampled by the agitated mushroom creatures in our cave. Would you mind bringing them [water] and protecting them from some of the fungus creatures? When you give generously and without expectations, you'll be surprised by the ways the world rewards you.'\nYou say, 'I can water them.'\nKejaan Kerrath says, 'That's excellent news. Please, take this decanter of water. There's a decent number of petunias growing in this cave, but I'd be happy if you watered just three of them. In fact, there's one in this room, next to those rocks. You can tell them apart from other flowers because of their radiating orange and pink petals. Take care not to overwater them; that's just as bad as not watering them at all. I've got more stories and lessons for you once you've finished this task.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'A Lesson in Altruism'.\nYou are given: Decanter of Cavern Water\n\n---\n\nLong, long ago, kerrans did not live harmoniously on Odus. Tribes fought against tribes to claim as much of the land as they could. The coasts and forest were nothing more than depletable resources, and the kerran tribes' battle for dominion over Odus threatened to forever change the ecosystem they lived in. Kejaan Kerrath has pointed out that all relationships are give and take. If you continuously take from the life around you without giving back, one day you'll find yourself with nothing left to take from. Kejaan has encouraged you to give back to the environment that you've been taking from: he wants you to take care of some of the rare flowers in Darklight Caverns.\n1\\. Water 3 nightlight petunias in Darklight Caverns 0/3 Darklight Caverns\n> **Quest Text:** Locate three nightlight petunias and water them using the decanter of cavern water. Protext the flowers from some of the mushroom creatures who might trample them.\n_Find a nightlight petunia in Darklight Caverns. They look like big sunflowers with red petals. You can find them all along the water edges. Get close and right click the Decanter of Cavern Water on them. If successful, you'll see the below._\nYour task 'A Lesson in Altruism' has been updated.\nThe petunia's leaves perk up as you water the soil.\nThe petunia's petals unfurl and reveal small fruit for you to pick.\n_You'll get this when the flower cannot be watered anymore._\nThe soil is already damp. You can water this petunia later, when the ground dries.\n_Once all 3 petunias are watered, you'll be given the fruit automatically._\nYou have been given: Nightlight Petunia Fruit\n2\\. Dispatch 5 mushroom creatures 0/5 Darklight Caverns\n> **Quest Text:** Protect the flowers from some of the mushroom creatures who might trample them. Return the decanter to Kejaan Kerrath. Give the nightlight fruit to Kejaan so that he may inspect it.\n_Most mushroom creatures should count for this part._\nKill 5 mushroom mobs\nYour task 'A Lesson in Altruism' has been updated.\n3\\. Return the decanter to Kejaan Kerrath 0/1 Darklight Caverns\nYou offered 1 Decanter of Cavern Water to Kejaan Kerrath.\nYour task 'A Lesson in Altruism' has been updated.\nKejaan Kerrath says, 'Excellent!'\nYou complete the trade with Kejaan Kerrath.\n4\\. Give the nightlight fruit to Kejaan Kerrath 0/1 Darklight Caverns\nYou offered 1 Nightlight Petunia Fruit to Kejaan Kerrath.\nYour task 'A Lesson in Altruism' has been updated.\nKejaan Kerrath says, 'What's this? I had no idea the nightlight petunias bore fruit! Just another testament to the power of give and take. You gave them water, and the flowers reciprocated your generosity. Let me hold on to this. I think it will come in handy later.'\nYou complete the trade with Kejaan Kerrath.\nYou have received a replay timer for 'A Lesson in Altruism': 0d:1h:0m remaining.\nKejaan looks like he wants to tell another story.\n\n---\n\nReward(s):\nMoney\nExperience\n**Submitted by:** Gidono",
