y say, then that land belongs to you. The spirits have said so. Karani, Shahar, and I will share the land currently under our paws.' They accepted the spirits' prophecy, and thus began the [splintering] of the four.'\nYou say, 'Splintering?'\nKejaan Kerrath says, 'Each of the four claimed a part of Odus. Kajek remained on the Stonebrunt Mountains. Shahar moved to the fruitful plains in the north. Karani lived on the coast. Shir was left with a rocky, barren stretch of land. Over time, most kerrans came to [live] within one of these clans.'\nYou say, 'But the four did not live side-by-side?'\nKejaan Kerrath says, 'No. The children of Kajek, Karani, Shahar, and Shir took over leading their respective clans. Each child hoped to be the 'Wise One' from the prophecy and thus become the leader of all kerrans. Their arrogance started wars that led to thousands of deaths. Their folly can [educate] us on a valuable lesson.'\nYou say, 'Educate me.'\nKejaan Kerrath says, 'Kerrans believe that life is like a mirror; it reflects back what you put in front of it. Smile at the mirror and the world smiles back. Look upon it with anger, and you will see only anger. The enmity between the clan leaders was reflected in the [communities] they led. The kerrans were irate and exhausted. The joy was sapped from them.'\nYou say, 'Could the communities recover?'\nKejaan Kerrath says, 'Fortunately, all things can grow and heal if they are treated with care. Around this room, you may have noticed the sullen animal spirits. The years they've been trapped has left them shades of their former selves. Would you [cheer] them up? Remember: life is like a mirror. Show the world kindness, and it will return that emotion.'\nYou say, 'I will cheer them up.'\nKejaan Kerrath says, 'Thank you, Shabu. Though these spirits do not speak common, actions can speak louder than words.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'A Lesson in Healing'.\n\n---\n\nAll steps received at once.\n1\\. Ease Airella's Cries 0/1 Darklight Caverns\nYou say, 'Hail, Airella, a weeping spirit'\nUse /comfort while targeting Airella.\nYou comfort Airella, a weeping spirit.\nYour task 'A Lesson in Healing' has been updated.\nAirella's shoulders relax. She stops baying and instead looks at you. Her ears perk up as you comfort her.\nYou say, 'Hail, Airella, a weeping spirit'\nAirella, now comforted, wags her tail when she looks at you.\n2\\. Quell Ralion's apprehension 0/1 Darklight Caverns\nYou say, 'Hail, Ralion, an apprehensive spirit'\nUse /calm while targeting Ralion.\nYou try to calm down Ralion, an apprehensive spirit.\nYour task 'A Lesson in Healing' has been updated.\nRallion slowly stops growling. He sits back on his haunches and looks at you with calm curiosity.\nYou say, 'Hail, Ralion, an apprehensive spirit'\nRallion, now calmed, watches you with quiet composure.\n3\\. Soothe Veeras' loneliness 0/1 Darklight Caverns\nYou say, 'Hail, Veeras, a lonesome spirit'\nVeeras, a lonesome spirit, nudges his head against your hand and looks at you with pleading eyes.\nUse /pat while targeting Veeras.\nYou pat Veeras, a lonesome spirit on the back.\nYour task 'A Lesson in Healing' has been updated.\nVeeras' tail wags with unbridled joy.\nYou say, 'Hail, Veeras, a lonesome spirit'\nVeeras, no longer lonely, wags his tail as you approach. He leans toward you, hoping for a pat.\n4\\. Console Boyo 0/1 Darklight Caverns\nYou say, 'Hail, Boyo, a pining spirit'\nBoyo, a pining spirit, grumbles. He sits back and raises his arms toward you, but it doesn't look like he wants to attack.\nUse /hug while targeting Boyo.\nYou hug Boyo, a pining spirit.\nYour task 'A Lesson in Healing' has been updated.\nBoyo accepts your hug. He rests his head and arms on your shoulders. Despite being a spirit, he is quite heavy.\nYou say, 'Hail, Boyo, a pining spirit'\nBoyo, now given affection, looks relaxed and happy at your presence.\n5\\. Check in with Linola 0/1 Darklight Caverns\nYou say, 'Hail, Linola, an eager spirit'\nLinola, an eager spirit, yips to get your attention, as though in greeting. She holds her tail upright and wags it back and forth.\nUse /wave while targeting Linola.\nYou wave at Linola, an eager spirit.\nYour task 'A Lesson in Healing' has been updated.\nLinola barks with excitement. She moves toward you and tries to lick your face.\nYou say, 'Hail, Linola, an eager spirit'\nLinola, now that you've waved at her, barks in greeting when she sees you.\n6\\. Relieve Zuura's boredom 0/1 Darklight Caverns\nYou say, 'Hail, Zuura, a bored spirit'\nUse /dance while targeting Zuura.\nYou grab hold of Zuura, a bored spirit and begin to dance with it.\nYour task 'A Lesson in Healing' has been updated.\nZuura lets out a happy howl. Her tail wags so hard that her body wiggles with it.\nYou say, 'Hail, Zuura, a bored spirit'\nZuura, now entertained, jumps up happily when you approach her.\n7\\. Find out what Mynosa wants 0/1 Darklight Caverns\nYou say, 'Hail, Mynosa, a proud spirit'\nMynosa, a proud spirit, examines you with interest. She looks regal. When you address her, she dips her head down, holds it, then raises it.\nUse /bow while targeting Mynosa.\nYou bow before Mynosa, a proud spirit.\nYour task 'A Lesson in Healing' has been updated.\nMynosa's ears perk when you bow to her. She nods her head and seems pleased.\nYou say, 'Hail, Mynosa, a proud spirit'\nMynosa, now that you've properly addressed her, bows in cordial greeting.\n8\\. Report to Kejaan Kerrath 0/1 Darklight Caverns\nHail Kejaan.\nYou say, 'Hail, Kejaan Kerrath'\nYour task 'A Lesson in Healing' has been updated.\nKejaan Kerrath says, 'The mood in this room has lightened up considerably! Thank you for treating the spirits with such kindness. I think the saying about mirrors rings true. Put positive energy into the world and the world reflects it back. There is one [extra thing] I hope you can help with.'\nYou say, 'What is the extra thing?'\nKejaan Kerrath says, 'Some creatures in this cavern contribute only negative energy. I am thinking specifically of the spiders who live in the cave to my left. They're violent creatures who threaten to expand their webs through the entirety of Darklight Caverns if not kept in check. Could you [cull their population] a bit?'\nYou say, 'I will cull their population.'\nKejaan Kerrath clasps his hands together in joy. 'You are doing us a great service, Shabu. Come see me when you are done. There's one part left to my story.'\n9\\. Kill 6 spiders 0/6 Darklight Caverns\nKill 6 of the spiders who threaten to overtake the cave.\nThere are spiders located in the north east portion of the zone, kill 6 of them.\nYour task 'A Lesson in Healing' has been updated.\n10\\. Speak again to Kejaan Kerrath 0/1 Darklight Caverns\nReport back to Kejaan Kerrath.\nYou say, 'Hail, Kejaan Kerrath'\nYour task 'A Lesson in Healing' has been updated.\nYou have received a replay timer for 'A Lesson in Healing': 0d:1h:0m remaining.\nKejaan Kerrath smiles warmly at you.\nYou receive 4 copper .\nYou receive 8 silver .\nYou receive 177 platinum .\nYou gain experience!\nKejaan Kerrath says, 'You're strong, Hayate! Thank you for putting a stop to the spiders' growing nest, even if it's only a temporary solution. Rest here as much as you need, or let me know if you'd like another task.'\n\n---\n\nReward(s):\n177p 8s 4cp\nExperience",
